// KI-2 regression demo — an effectful call bound and returned bare in tail
// position, after a dropped binding, must be emitted once on the native backend
// (see docs/internals/known_issues.md, Resolved: KI-2).
//
// `Lib.m` has the shape `drop cid in (let r = f(never()); r)`. Before the fix,
// the aether reuse pass followed the `r -> f(never())` alias and substituted the
// call into the body position while keeping the binding, producing
// `let r = f(never()) in f(never())` — so the native backend emitted `f` (and
// `never`) twice, the first result discarded. This is an IR-level bug: with the
// `print` effect below it is masked (the effect handler runs it once on both
// backends), so stdout is "F"/42 either way. Inspect the lowering to see the fix:
//
//     cargo run --features llvm -- --dump-lir \
//         examples/aether/regression_ki2_reuse_drop_let/main.flx --native
//
// Before the fix `Lib_m` had two `call` sites for `f`/`never`; now it has one.
// The behavioral guard is the unit test
// reuse_analysis::tests::effectful_let_returned_bare_is_not_duplicated.
//
// Runs on both backends (prints "F" then 42):
//
//     cargo run -- examples/aether/regression_ki2_reuse_drop_let/main.flx
//     cargo native   examples/aether/regression_ki2_reuse_drop_let/main.flx

// parity-expected-stdout-begin
// "F"
// 42
// parity-expected-stdout-end

import Lib exposing (..)
import Flow.Event exposing (Event)

fn ff(e: Event<Int>) -> Int with IO {
    print("F")
    42
}

fn main() with IO {
    print(m(ff))
}
